IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eca-nouns`
IMPORT `eca-schedules`
IMPORT `eca-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `eca-part2-mediation`
IMPORT `eca-part3-jurisdiction`
IMPORT `eca-part3-proceedings`
IMPORT `eca-part3-appeals`
IMPORT `eca-part4-miscellaneous`

-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 April 2025 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: an employee, or a former employee, with a salary-related claim against an employer, asking on facts they can state whether they may bring it to the tribunal, in what time, with what steps and at what cost, and what follows.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.  Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the modules' inputs from the person's answers and calls the module's own function.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure" (`My answer`); "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A date is asked as day, month and year; any of them given as 0 means "I do not know", and becomes NOTHING.
--   * An amount, a period or a limit that regulations, Rules of Court or practice directions set is asked as a number; 0 means "I do not know" and becomes NOTHING.  (So a fee that is really nil cannot be stated, and is read as not known: the safe direction, "not covered".)
--   * The Act's own periods (6 months, one month, 2 months, one year, 14 days) are taken from the modules.  A Minister's order under s 3(7) could change the periods in s 3(2) and would change the answers.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- ONE ANSWER PER SECTION (ruling E1, option C).  Whether the tribunal may hear my claim is answered requirement by requirement -- s 12(2), (3), (4), (5), (6), (7) -- and ss 3, 16 and 28 each answer for themselves.  The question at the end of that group, s 12(1), takes the person's own answers to those and gathers them by hand; it is a convenience and not a different rule.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Where a provision addresses only an official (ss 8, 9, 10, 11, 32, 33, 34, 35(1)) the rule is in layer 1 or is machinery, and the person meets it only through the questions below.

DECLARE `My answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- A date from what the person knows: a day, month or year given as 0 means not known.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`my date if I know it` MEANS
    IF day EQUALS 0 OR month EQUALS 0 OR year EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (Date day month year) -- input mapping

-- A date the person must give (the question cannot be asked without it).
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`my date` MEANS
    Date day month year -- input mapping

-- The facts s 3(2) needs, from one date: the person gives the single date their time limit counts from (see the question), and it is placed in every slot; the module picks the slot the kind of dispute needs.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of dispute for the time limit`
      ended IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts for the mediation request time limit`
`my facts for the time limit` MEANS
    `Facts for the mediation request time limit` WITH
        kind IS kind -- input mapping
        `the employment relationship has ended` IS ended -- input mapping
        `the last day of the period in section 65(2A) of the Employment Act 1968, as extended under section 65(2B)` IS d -- input mapping
        `the last day of employment of the employee` IS d -- input mapping
        `the last day of the time determined under section 8B(8) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` IS d -- input mapping
        `the date of the dismissal of the employee` IS d -- input mapping
        `the date of the employee's confinement` IS d -- input mapping
        `the date on which the material facts giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute listed in the mediation request occurred` IS d -- input mapping

§ `The Employment Claims Act 2016 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Must I ask for mediation first, and by when? (ss 3 and 4)`
-- Situation: asked of every employee or former employee who has a salary-related dispute and wants to bring it to the tribunal.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 3(1) and (8).  Before lodging a claim you must submit a mediation request to the Commissioner, unless a tripartite mediation has already been conducted.
@export Must I submit a mediation request before I lodge my claim (s 3(1) and (8))?
GIVEN `my claim will be lodged for a specified employment dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will your claim be lodged for a specified employment dispute (a salary or similar money dispute under your contract of service, a dispute under one of the Acts in the Second Schedule, or a wrongful dismissal dispute)?
      `a tripartite mediation has already been conducted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a tripartite mediation already been conducted to try to settle the disputes your claim is about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I submit a mediation request first` IS
    `s 3(1) the claimant must submit a mediation request before lodging the claim` `my claim will be lodged for a specified employment dispute` `a tripartite mediation has already been conducted`

-- s 3(1).  The mediation request must relate to every specified employment dispute your claim will be lodged for.
@export Does my mediation request cover every dispute my claim will be lodged for (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `the number of disputes my claim will be lodged for` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many specified employment disputes will your claim be lodged?
      `the number of those disputes my request relates to` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of them does your mediation request ask for mediation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my request cover every dispute` IS
    `s 3(1) the mediation request relates to every specified employment dispute for which the claim will be lodged` `the number of disputes my claim will be lodged for` `the number of those disputes my request relates to`

-- s 3(2).  The last day for the request depends on what the dispute is about.  Give the one date that your time limit counts from: for a salary-recovery dispute under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968, the last day of the period that section 65(2A) allows (as extended under 65(2B)); for a re-employment dispute under section 8B(7) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993, the last day of the time fixed under its section 8B(8); for wrongful dismissal, the date of the dismissal (or of the confinement, for a claim under section 84(2)); for any other dispute, the last day of your employment if it has ended, otherwise the date the material facts happened.
@export By what date must I submit my mediation request (s 3(2))?
GIVEN `what my dispute is about` IS A `Kind of dispute for the time limit` @desc What is your dispute about? (a recovery of salary under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968; a re-employment dispute under section 8A(3) or 8B(7) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993; a wrongful dismissal dispute under section 14(2) or 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968; or another specified employment dispute)
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employment ended?
      `the day my time limit counts from` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month is the date your time limit counts from? (0 if you do not know)
      `the month my time limit counts from` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 for January to 12 for December, is the date your time limit counts from? (0 if you do not know)
      `the year my time limit counts from` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year is the date your time limit counts from? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I submit my request` IS
    `s 3(2) the last day by which the mediation request must be submitted` (`my facts for the time limit` `what my dispute is about` `my employment has ended` (`my date if I know it` `the day my time limit counts from` `the month my time limit counts from` `the year my time limit counts from`))

-- s 3(2).  Is a request submitted on a given date in time?  The last day itself is in time.
@export Is my mediation request in time if I submit it on this date (s 3(2))?
GIVEN `what my dispute is about` IS A `Kind of dispute for the time limit` @desc What is your dispute about? (see the previous question for the choices)
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employment ended?
      `the day my time limit counts from` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month is the date your time limit counts from? (0 if you do not know)
      `the month my time limit counts from` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 for January to 12 for December, is the date your time limit counts from? (0 if you do not know)
      `the year my time limit counts from` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year is the date your time limit counts from? (0 if you do not know)
      `the day I submit the request` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month do you submit (or did you submit) your mediation request?
      `the month I submit the request` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, do you submit (or did you submit) your mediation request?
      `the year I submit the request` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year do you submit (or did you submit) your mediation request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my request in time` IS
    `s 3(2) the mediation request is submitted by the time` (`s 3(2) the last day by which the mediation request must be submitted` (`my facts for the time limit` `what my dispute is about` `my employment has ended` (`my date if I know it` `the day my time limit counts from` `the month my time limit counts from` `the year my time limit counts from`))) (`my date` `the day I submit the request` `the month I submit the request` `the year I submit the request`)

-- s 3(3)(a).  The request must list every specified employment dispute for which the three requirements are met.
@export Must my mediation request list this dispute (s 3(3)(a))?
GIVEN `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a claim for an amount of money relating to this dispute?
      `that claim meets the requirements of section 12(2), (3) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that claim meet the requirements of section 12(2), (3) and (4) (the right people, the right kind of claim, and each amount relating to a specified employment dispute)? Answer Yes if there is no such claim.
      `the day the material facts happened` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month did the material facts giving rise to the dispute happen?
      `the month the material facts happened` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, did the material facts giving rise to the dispute happen?
      `the year the material facts happened` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year did the material facts giving rise to the dispute happen?
      `the day I submit the request` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month do you submit your mediation request?
      `the month I submit the request` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, do you submit your mediation request?
      `the year I submit the request` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year do you submit your mediation request?
      `it is listed in an earlier accepted request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this dispute listed in an earlier mediation request between you and the same respondent that the Commissioner has already accepted?
      `it was withdrawn before the first session` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was it withdrawn before the date of the first mediation session under that earlier request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my request list this dispute` IS
    `s 3(3)(a) the mediation request must list the specified employment dispute` `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` `that claim meets the requirements of section 12(2), (3) and (4)` (`my date` `the day the material facts happened` `the month the material facts happened` `the year the material facts happened`) (`my date` `the day I submit the request` `the month I submit the request` `the year I submit the request`) `it is listed in an earlier accepted request` `it was withdrawn before the first session`

-- s 3(3)(c).  The request must not list a dispute if there is a claim for an amount relating to it and, under section 16, that claim cannot be lodged with a tribunal.
@export Must my mediation request leave this dispute out because the claim cannot be lodged (s 3(3)(c))?
GIVEN `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a claim for an amount of money relating to this dispute?
      `section 16 bars lodging that claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 16 mean that this claim cannot be lodged with a tribunal (for example, because the same matter is already before another court, or you made representations to a Minister)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my request leave this dispute out` IS
    `s 3(3)(c) the mediation request must not list the specified employment dispute` `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` `section 16 bars lodging that claim`

-- s 3(3)(d).  The request must be accompanied by the prescribed fee.  The fee is set by regulations, so you give it.
@export Is the fee I am paying with my mediation request enough (s 3(3)(d))?
GIVEN `the fee I am paying` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, are you paying as the fee with your mediation request?
      `the fee the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What fee, in dollars, do the regulations prescribe for a mediation under Part 2 of the Act? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my mediation fee enough` IS
    `s 3(3)(d) the mediation request is accompanied by the prescribed fee` `the fee I am paying` (`my amount if I know it` `the fee the regulations prescribe`)

-- s 3(4)(a).  The Commissioner may refuse to accept the request if it does not comply with s 3(2) and (3), or the requirement in s 12(7) cannot be satisfied for the claim.
@export Can the Commissioner refuse to accept my mediation request (s 3(4)(a))?
GIVEN `my request complies with the time and content requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request comply with section 3(2) (in time) and section 3(3) (lists and leaves out the right disputes, with the fee)?
      `the claim limit can be met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the requirement in section 12(7) (that the total claimed is within the claim limit) be satisfied for your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commissioner refuse my request` IS
    `s 3(4)(a) the Commissioner may refuse to accept the mediation request` `my request complies with the time and content requirements` `the claim limit can be met`

-- s 3(4)(b).  The Commissioner may waive, remit or refund the fee, wholly or in part.  The grant has no condition.
@export May the Commissioner waive, remit or refund my mediation fee (s 3(4)(b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my mediation fee be waived` IS
    `s 3(4)(b) the Commissioner may waive, remit or refund the fee`

-- s 3(5).  Once the Commissioner accepts the request, the Commissioner must refer each listed dispute to an approved mediator as soon as reasonably practicable.
@export Must the Commissioner refer my dispute to an approved mediator once my request is accepted (s 3(5))?
GIVEN `the Commissioner has accepted my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner accepted your mediation request?
      `the dispute is listed in my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this dispute listed in your request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner refer my dispute to a mediator` IS
    `s 3(5) the Commissioner must refer the specified employment dispute for mediation by an approved mediator` `the Commissioner has accepted my request` `the dispute is listed in my request`

-- s 3(6)(b).  Regulations may prescribe the persons, or classes of persons, who may submit a mediation request on a claimant's behalf.
@export May someone else submit my mediation request for me (s 3(6)(b))?
GIVEN `that person is prescribed to submit on my behalf` IS A `My answer` @desc Do the regulations prescribe the person who would submit for you, or a class of persons they belong to, as persons who may submit a mediation request on a claimant's behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May someone submit my request for me` IS
    `s 3(6)(b) the person may submit the mediation request on behalf of the claimant` (`what I say, as a fact` `that person is prescribed to submit on my behalf`)

-- s 4(1).  The approved mediator must conduct the first session as soon as reasonably practicable after the dispute is referred.
@export Must the approved mediator hold the first mediation session (s 4(1))?
GIVEN `my dispute has been referred to the mediator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your dispute been referred to the approved mediator (by the Commissioner under section 3(5), or by a court or the tribunal under section 7(5)(b)(ii) or 22(8))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the mediator hold the first session` IS
    `s 4(1) the approved mediator must conduct the first mediation session` `my dispute has been referred to the mediator`

-- s 4(2).  The mediator need not conduct any session if satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settling the dispute through mediation.
@export May the mediator decide not to hold any mediation session (s 4(2))?
GIVEN `the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the approved mediator satisfied that there is no reasonable prospect of settling your dispute through mediation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the mediator decide not to hold a session` IS
    `s 4(2) the approved mediator need not conduct a mediation session` `the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement`

-- s 4(3).  Each mediation session must be held in private.
@export Must my mediation session be held in private (s 4(3))?
GIVEN `it is a mediation session under Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a mediation session under Part 2 of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my mediation session private` IS
    `s 4(3) the mediation session must be held in private` `it is a mediation session under Part 2`

-- s 4(4) and (5).  The same mediator may take disputes together in three cases.
@export May the same mediator take my dispute together with others (s 4(4) and (5))?
GIVEN `two or more claimants have the same respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have two or more claimants submitted requests about specified employment disputes with the same respondent?
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the disputes are similar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is the Commissioner satisfied that all those disputes are similar in nature?
      `we claim against each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you and the other side intend to lodge claims against each other, and has each of you submitted a request?
      `I have several requests for the same salary against different respondents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you submitted two or more requests about the recovery of the same salary under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968 against different respondents?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the same mediator take my dispute with others` IS
    `s 4(4) the same approved mediator may take the disputes together` (`s 4(5) subsection (4) applies` `two or more claimants have the same respondent` `the Commissioner is satisfied the disputes are similar` `we claim against each other` `I have several requests for the same salary against different respondents`)

-- s 5(1) to (3).  At a mediation you act in person and cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor or by an agent, except as s 5(2) and (3) allow.
@export Can this person represent me, or the other side, at the mediation (s 5(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `who the party is` IS A `Kind of party` @desc Who is the party to be represented? (an individual; the Government; a body corporate; a partnership; an unincorporated association)
      `who would represent the party` IS A `Kind of representative` @desc Who would represent the party?
      `the regulations prescribe this representative for this party` IS A `My answer` @desc Do the regulations made under section 34 prescribe this individual as a representative for this party? (Answer only if the representative is "another individual prescribed by regulations".)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this person represent a party at the mediation` IS
    `s 5(1) to (3) the party may be represented at the mediation by the representative` `who the party is` `who would represent the party` (`what I say, as a fact` `the regulations prescribe this representative for this party`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Will I get a claim referral certificate? (s 6)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 6(1) and (4).  A dispute is unresolved if it is not settled and not withdrawn from the list.
@export Is my dispute still unresolved (s 6(4))?
GIVEN `my dispute is settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your dispute been settled?
      `my dispute was withdrawn from the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your dispute been withdrawn from the list of specified employment disputes in your mediation request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my dispute unresolved` IS
    `s 6(4) the specified employment dispute is unresolved` `my dispute is settled` `my dispute was withdrawn from the list`

-- s 6(2).  The approved mediator must issue the claimant a certificate for every unresolved dispute if the respondent, given reasonable notice, does not attend; no settlement is reached; or the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement.
@export Must the mediator give me a claim referral certificate for this dispute (s 6(2))?
GIVEN `I submitted a mediation request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit a mediation request to the Commissioner?
      `the Commissioner referred this dispute to a mediator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commissioner refer this dispute, listed in your request, to an approved mediator?
      `my dispute is settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your dispute been settled?
      `my dispute was withdrawn from the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your dispute been withdrawn from the list of specified employment disputes in your mediation request?
      `the other side was given notice and did not attend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the respondent given reasonable notice of the mediation and did not attend?
      `no settlement was reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no settlement reached at the end of the mediation of one or more of the disputes listed?
      `the mediator is satisfied there is no prospect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the approved mediator satisfied that there is no reasonable prospect of settling the dispute through mediation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the mediator give me a certificate` IS
    `s 6(2) the approved mediator must issue the claimant a claim referral certificate for the dispute` (`s 6(1) section 6 applies` `I submitted a mediation request` `the Commissioner referred this dispute to a mediator`) (`s 6(4) the specified employment dispute is unresolved` `my dispute is settled` `my dispute was withdrawn from the list`) `the other side was given notice and did not attend` `no settlement was reached` `the mediator is satisfied there is no prospect`

-- s 6(3).  If you submit a request but, without reasonable excuse, fail to attend any session, the mediator may discontinue the mediation and refuse to issue a certificate.
@export Can the mediator discontinue the mediation and refuse me a certificate because I did not attend (s 6(3))?
GIVEN `I submitted a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit the mediation request?
      `I missed a session without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail, without reasonable excuse, to attend a mediation session to which your request relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the mediator refuse me a certificate` IS
    `s 6(3) the approved mediator may discontinue the mediation and refuse to issue a claim referral certificate` `I submitted a request` `I missed a session without reasonable excuse`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If my dispute settles at mediation (s 7)`
-- Situation: asked only of a person whose dispute has been settled at a mediation under Part 2 or a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 7(1)(a).  The parties must enter into a settlement agreement in the form prescribed by Rules of Court.
@export Is my settlement agreement in the form the Rules of Court prescribe (s 7(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my dispute was settled at a mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your dispute settled at a mediation under Part 2, or at a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator?
      `the agreement is in the prescribed form` IS A `My answer` @desc Is your settlement agreement in the form that the Rules of Court prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my settlement agreement in the prescribed form` IS
    `s 7(1)(a) the settlement agreement is in the form prescribed` `my dispute was settled at a mediation` (`what I say, as a fact` `the agreement is in the prescribed form`)

-- s 7(1)(b).  The total payable to a party for contractual and statutory disputes must not exceed the prescribed claim limit.
@export Is the most I can be paid for salary-type disputes in my settlement within the claim limit (s 7(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my dispute was settled at a mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your dispute settled at a mediation under Part 2, or at a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator?
      `the total payable to me for these disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, is payable to you under the settlement agreement for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute settled?
      `the claim limit for these disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my settlement within the claim limit for salary-type disputes` IS
    `s 7(1)(b) the total amount payable to the party for contractual and statutory disputes is within the limit` `my dispute was settled at a mediation` `the total payable to me for these disputes` (`my amount if I know it` `the claim limit for these disputes`)

-- s 7(1)(c).  The same for wrongful dismissal disputes.
@export Is the total payable to me for wrongful dismissal in my settlement within the claim limit (s 7(1)(c))?
GIVEN `my dispute was settled at a mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your dispute settled at a mediation under Part 2, or at a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator?
      `the total payable to me for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, is payable to you under the settlement agreement for every wrongful dismissal dispute settled?
      `the claim limit for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my settlement within the claim limit for wrongful dismissal` IS
    `s 7(1)(c) the total amount payable to the party for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the limit` `my dispute was settled at a mediation` `the total payable to me for wrongful dismissal` (`my amount if I know it` `the claim limit for wrongful dismissal`)

-- s 7(1)(d).  The settlement agreement must be signed by or on behalf of each party.
@export Is my settlement agreement signed as the Act requires (s 7(1)(d))?
GIVEN `my dispute was settled at a mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your dispute settled at a mediation under Part 2, or at a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator?
      `the number of parties` IS A NUMBER @desc How many parties are there to the settlement agreement?
      `the number of parties who signed` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many parties has the agreement been signed (by the party or on the party's behalf)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my settlement agreement signed by or for every party` IS
    `s 7(1)(d) the settlement agreement is signed by or on behalf of each party` `my dispute was settled at a mediation` `the number of parties` `the number of parties who signed`

-- s 7(2).  A District Court may register the agreement on any party's application.
@export May a District Court register my settlement agreement (s 7(2))?
GIVEN `a party applies to a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a party to the settlement agreement applied to a District Court to register it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a District Court register my settlement agreement` IS
    `s 7(2) a District Court may register the settlement agreement` `a party applies to a District Court`

-- s 7(2).  But the Court may refuse to register if the application is not made within the period the Rules of Court prescribe.
@export May a District Court refuse to register my settlement agreement because my application is late (s 7(2))?
GIVEN `my application was made in the prescribed period` IS A `My answer` @desc Was the application made within the period that the Rules of Court prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a District Court refuse because the application is late` IS
    `s 7(2) a District Court may refuse to register the settlement agreement` (`what I say, as a fact` `my application was made in the prescribed period`)

-- s 7(3)(a).  Once registered, the agreement has the force and effect of a District Court judgment entered on the date of registration.
@export From what date does my registered settlement agreement have the force of a judgment (s 7(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the agreement is registered in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your settlement agreement been registered in a District Court?
      `the day it was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was it registered?
      `the month it was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, was it registered?
      `the year it was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year was it registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what date does my registered agreement have the force of a judgment` IS
    `s 7(3)(a) the date from which the settlement agreement has the force and effect of a judgment for execution or enforcement` `the agreement is registered in a District Court` (`my date` `the day it was registered` `the month it was registered` `the year it was registered`)

-- s 7(3)(b) and (c).  Once registered, proceedings may be taken on it as on a judgment, and the registered amount carries interest as a judgment debt.
@export Can I take proceedings on my registered settlement agreement as on a judgment (s 7(3)(b))?
GIVEN `the agreement is registered in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your settlement agreement been registered in a District Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take proceedings on my registered agreement` IS
    `s 7(3)(b) proceedings may be taken on the settlement agreement as on a judgment` `the agreement is registered in a District Court`

@export Does the amount in my registered settlement agreement carry interest as a judgment debt (s 7(3)(c))?
GIVEN `the agreement is registered in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your settlement agreement been registered in a District Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my registered amount carry interest` IS
    `s 7(3)(c) an amount for which the settlement agreement is registered carries interest as a judgment debt` `the agreement is registered in a District Court`

-- s 7(4).  After registration a party may apply to a District Court to set the registration aside, within the period the Rules of Court prescribe.
@export May I apply to a District Court to set aside the registration of my settlement agreement (s 7(4))?
GIVEN `the agreement is registered in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the settlement agreement been registered in a District Court?
      `my application is within the prescribed period` IS A `My answer` @desc Is your application made within the period that the Rules of Court prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to set aside the registration` IS
    `s 7(4) a party may apply to set aside the registration` `the agreement is registered in a District Court` (`what I say, as a fact` `my application is within the prescribed period`)

-- s 7(5) and (6).  The Court may set aside the registration and the agreement if a condition in s 7(6) is satisfied.
@export Can a District Court set aside my settlement agreement (s 7(5) and (6))?
GIVEN `it is void or voidable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the settlement agreement void or voidable on a ground that invalidates a contract (incapacity, fraud, misrepresentation, duress, coercion, mistake or any other)?
      `it covers subject matter outside the disputes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include subject matter that does not relate to a specified employment dispute?
      `a term cannot be enforced as a court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a term of it not capable of enforcement as an order of a District Court?
      `registration is against public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is registering it contrary to public policy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a District Court set aside my settlement agreement` IS
    `s 7(5)(b)(i) a District Court may set aside the settlement agreement` (`s 7(6) a condition for setting aside is satisfied` `it is void or voidable` `it covers subject matter outside the disputes` `a term cannot be enforced as a court order` `registration is against public policy`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `May I bring my claim to the tribunal? (ss 12 to 17)`
-- Each requirement is answered on its own (ruling E1); the last question in this group gathers them.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 12(2)(a) and (b).  The claim must be made by an employee (or the person entitled in the employee's place) against the employer, or against a person liable under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968 for the salary; the employee must be prescribed or in a prescribed class.
@export Is my claim made by and against the right people (s 12(2))?
GIVEN `who is making the claim` IS A `Who makes the claim` @desc Who is making the claim? (you as the employee; a person entitled by a written law to receive the amount in your place; or someone else)
      `who the claim is against` IS A `Whom the claim is made against` @desc Whom is the claim made against? (your employer; a person liable under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968 for your salary; or someone else)
      `I am in a prescribed class of employees` IS A `My answer` @desc Are you an employee who is prescribed, or who belongs to a class of employees that the regulations prescribe, for this kind of claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim made by and against the right people` IS
    `s 12(2) the claim is made as the subsection requires` (`s 12(2)(a) the claim is made by an employee in a prescribed class against the employer` `who is making the claim` `who the claim is against` (`what I say, as a fact` `I am in a prescribed class of employees`)) (`s 12(2)(b) the claim is made by an employee in a prescribed class against a person liable under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968` `who is making the claim` `who the claim is against` (`what I say, as a fact` `I am in a prescribed class of employees`)) (`s 12(2)(c) the claim is made by an employer in a prescribed class against an employee about a matter the paragraph names` `who is making the claim` `who the claim is against` `None of the matters in the Schedules` NOTHING NOTHING)

-- s 12(2)(c).  An employer may make a claim against an employee about a matter in item 17 of the First Schedule or item 14 or 16 of the Second Schedule, or about any other First or Second Schedule matter that is prescribed, if the employer is prescribed or belongs to a prescribed class.  This is how a claim by your employer against you is tested.
@export May my employer bring a claim against me about this matter (s 12(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the matter of my employer's claim` IS A `Matter of a dispute` @desc What is your employer's claim about? (a matter in the First Schedule such as salary in lieu of notice of termination, a matter in the Second Schedule such as the payments in items 14 and 16, a matter in the Third Schedule, or none of the matters in the Schedules)
      `my employer is in a prescribed class of employers` IS A `My answer` @desc Is your employer an employer who is prescribed, or who belongs to a class of employers that the regulations prescribe, for this kind of claim?
      `the matter is prescribed for this purpose` IS A `My answer` @desc If the matter is in the First or Second Schedule but is not one of the items 17, 14 or 16, do the regulations prescribe it for the purposes of section 12(2)(c)(ii)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer claim against me` IS
    `s 12(2)(c) the claim is made by an employer in a prescribed class against an employee about a matter the paragraph names` `The employer` `An employee of the employer` `the matter of my employer's claim` (`what I say, as a fact` `my employer is in a prescribed class of employers`) (`what I say, as a fact` `the matter is prescribed for this purpose`)

-- s 12(3).  The claim must be for amounts alleged to be payable to you, or (in a wrongful dismissal case) reinstatement, or both.
@export Is my claim for what the Act allows a tribunal claim to be for (s 12(3))?
GIVEN `my claim is for amounts payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for one or more amounts alleged to be payable to you by the respondent?
      `my claim is for reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for reinstatement in your former employment?
      `my claim is about wrongful dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim lodged in respect of a wrongful dismissal dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim the kind the Act allows` IS
    `s 12(3) the claim is for what the subsection requires` `my claim is for amounts payable to me` `my claim is for reinstatement` `my claim is about wrongful dismissal`

-- s 12(4).  Each amount you claim must relate to a specified employment dispute.
@export Does each amount I claim relate to a specified employment dispute (s 12(4))?
GIVEN `the number of amounts I claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How many separate amounts do you claim?
      `the number that relate to a specified employment dispute` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those amounts relate to a specified employment dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does each amount relate to a specified employment dispute` IS
    `s 12(4) each amount alleged to be payable relates to a specified employment dispute` `the number of amounts I claim` `the number that relate to a specified employment dispute`

-- s 12(5).  The claim must be supported by a claim referral certificate for every specified employment dispute it is lodged for.
@export Is my claim supported by a claim referral certificate for every dispute (s 12(5))?
GIVEN `the number of disputes my claim is lodged for` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many specified employment disputes is your claim lodged?
      `the number of those disputes with a certificate` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of them do you have a claim referral certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim supported by a certificate for every dispute` IS
    `s 12(5) the claim is supported by a claim referral certificate for every specified employment dispute` `the number of disputes my claim is lodged for` `the number of those disputes with a certificate`

-- s 12(6).  The claim must be lodged within the prescribed period after the date the certificate was issued.  The period is in regulations, so you give it.
@export Am I in time to lodge my claim after my certificate was issued (s 12(6))?
GIVEN `the day my certificate was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was your claim referral certificate issued?
      `the month my certificate was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, was it issued?
      `the year my certificate was issued` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year was it issued?
      `the day I lodge the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month do you lodge (or did you lodge) your claim?
      `the month I lodge the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, do you lodge (or did you lodge) your claim?
      `the year I lodge the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year do you lodge (or did you lodge) your claim?
      `the number of days the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the date of issue of the certificate do the regulations prescribe for lodging the claim? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to lodge my claim` IS
    `s 12(6) the claim is lodged within the prescribed period after the certificate was issued` (`my date` `the day my certificate was issued` `the month my certificate was issued` `the year my certificate was issued`) (`my date` `the day I lodge the claim` `the month I lodge the claim` `the year I lodge the claim`) (`my amount if I know it` `the number of days the regulations prescribe`)

-- s 12(7).  The totals claimed must not exceed the prescribed claim limits that apply to you.
@export Is the total I claim within the claim limits (s 12(7))?
GIVEN `the total I claim for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, do you claim for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute?
      `my claim limit for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
      `the total I claim for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, do you claim for every wrongful dismissal dispute? (0 if none)
      `my claim limit for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the total I claim within the claim limits` IS
    `s 12(7) the total amount alleged satisfies the conditions` (`s 12(7)(a) the total alleged for contractual and statutory disputes is within the claim limit` `the total I claim for salary-type disputes` (`my amount if I know it` `my claim limit for salary-type disputes`)) (`s 12(7)(b) the total alleged for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the claim limit` `the total I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`my amount if I know it` `my claim limit for wrongful dismissal`))

-- s 15(1).  If a total is over its limit, you may abandon the excess.
@export May I abandon the amount over the claim limit (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `the total I claim for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, do you claim for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute?
      `my claim limit for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
      `the total I claim for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, do you claim for every wrongful dismissal dispute? (0 if none)
      `my claim limit for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I abandon the excess` IS
    `s 15(1) the claimant may abandon the excess amount` `the total I claim for salary-type disputes` (`my amount if I know it` `my claim limit for salary-type disputes`) `the total I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`my amount if I know it` `my claim limit for wrongful dismissal`)

-- s 15(1)(a).  The excess is the amount by which the total for salary-type disputes is over its claim limit.
@export How much of my salary-type claim is over the claim limit (s 15(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the total I claim for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, do you claim for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute?
      `my claim limit for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the excess over the salary-type limit` IS
    `s 15(1)(a) the excess amount over the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a)` `the total I claim for salary-type disputes` (`my amount if I know it` `my claim limit for salary-type disputes`)

-- s 15(1)(b).  The excess is the amount by which the total for wrongful dismissal disputes is over its claim limit.
@export How much of my wrongful dismissal claim is over the claim limit (s 15(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the total I claim for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, do you claim for every wrongful dismissal dispute? (0 if none)
      `my claim limit for wrongful dismissal` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b) that applies to you, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the excess over the wrongful dismissal limit` IS
    `s 15(1)(b) the excess amount over the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(b)` `the total I claim for wrongful dismissal` (`my amount if I know it` `my claim limit for wrongful dismissal`)

-- s 15(2)(b).  If you abandon the excess, the tribunal has jurisdiction to hear the claim.
@export If I abandon the excess, does the tribunal have jurisdiction over my claim (s 15(2)(b))?
GIVEN `I abandon the excess amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you abandon the amount over the claim limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If I abandon the excess, may the tribunal hear my claim` IS
    `s 15(2)(b) section 15(2) gives the tribunal jurisdiction to hear and determine the claim` `I abandon the excess amount`

-- s 15(2)(c).  If you abandon the excess, an order on the claim fully discharges all demands in respect of it.
@export If I abandon the excess, does the tribunal's order fully discharge all demands for the claim (s 15(2)(c))?
GIVEN `I abandon the excess amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you abandon the amount over the claim limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If I abandon the excess, does the order discharge all demands` IS
    `s 15(2)(c) an order of the tribunal in relation to the claim fully discharges all demands in respect of the claim` `I abandon the excess amount`

-- s 15(3).  Once abandoned, the excess cannot be recovered in a tribunal or any other court.
@export Can I recover the amount I abandoned later (s 15(3))?
GIVEN `I have abandoned the excess amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you abandoned the amount over the claim limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I not recover the amount I abandoned` IS
    `s 15(3) the claimant cannot recover the excess amount in a tribunal or any other court` `I have abandoned the excess amount`

-- s 14.  A claim cannot be split into separate proceedings only to bring each part within the tribunal's jurisdiction.
@export Can I split my claim into separate proceedings (s 14)?
GIVEN `the only reason is to bring each part within the limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason for splitting your claim to bring the total in each of the separate proceedings within the jurisdiction of a tribunal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is splitting my claim barred` IS
    `s 14 the claim cannot be divided and pursued in separate proceedings before a tribunal` `the only reason is to bring each part within the limit`

-- s 16(1).  A claim cannot be lodged if proceedings about it are pending in, or decided by, another court or an Industrial Arbitration Court; or a claim under section 119 of the Employment Act 1968 is pending or the Commissioner decided the dispute under section 115.
@export Is my claim barred because it is already before another court or the Commissioner (s 16(1))?
GIVEN `proceedings about it are in or decided by another court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any proceedings about this claim pending in, or have they been heard and decided by, any other court or an Industrial Arbitration Court?
      `a claim under section 119 of the Employment Act is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a claim about this dispute pending under section 119 of the Employment Act 1968?
      `the Commissioner has decided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commissioner for Labour inquired into and decided this dispute under section 115 of the Employment Act 1968?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim barred by other proceedings` IS
    `s 16(1) the claim cannot be lodged with a tribunal` `proceedings about it are in or decided by another court` `a claim under section 119 of the Employment Act is pending` `the Commissioner has decided it`

-- s 16(2).  Once your claim is lodged, neither side can start proceedings about it in another court unless it is withdrawn, discontinued or dismissed for lack of jurisdiction.
@export Can either side start court proceedings about my claim after it is lodged (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `my claim is lodged with a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your claim been lodged with a tribunal?
      `it is withdrawn or discontinued or dismissed for lack of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the claim been withdrawn, discontinued or dismissed for lack of jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is starting other proceedings barred after I lodge` IS
    `s 16(2) no proceedings relating to the claim can be commenced in any other court or an Industrial Arbitration Court by either party against the other` `my claim is lodged with a tribunal` `it is withdrawn or discontinued or dismissed for lack of jurisdiction`

-- s 16(3).  After a dismissal, you cannot lodge a claim for salary in lieu of notice, or the payments in items 13 and 15 of the Second Schedule, if you made written representations to the Minister and have not withdrawn them, or the Minister has decided.
@export After my dismissal, am I barred from claiming salary in lieu of notice because I made representations to the Minister (s 16(3))?
GIVEN `I was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed?
      `the amount arises from the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amount you claim arise from that dismissal?
      `what my claim is about` IS A `Matter of a dispute` @desc What is the claim about? (a matter in the First Schedule such as salary in lieu of notice of termination, or a matter in the Second Schedule such as the payments in items 13 and 15)
      `what I wrote to the Minister` IS A `Representations to a Minister` @desc What representations in writing, if any, did you make to a Minister? (under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960; under section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993; under section 8B(1) of that Act; or none)
      `I withdrew them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw those representations?
      `the Minister decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister made a decision on those representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from lodging after making representations` IS
    `s 16(3) the employee cannot lodge the claim` `I was dismissed` `the amount arises from the dismissal` `what my claim is about` `what I wrote to the Minister` `I withdrew them` `the Minister decided`

-- s 16(4)(a) and (b).  If you lodged a claim and then made those representations, the claim is deemed discontinued from the date you made them.
@export Is the claim I lodged deemed discontinued because I then made representations to the Minister (s 16(4)(a))?
GIVEN `I was dismissed and have lodged a claim for an amount from the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed, and have you lodged a claim for an amount relating to a specified employment dispute that arises from the dismissal?
      `what my claim is about` IS A `Matter of a dispute` @desc What is the claim about? (a matter in the First Schedule such as salary in lieu of notice of termination, or a matter in the Second Schedule such as the payments in items 13 and 15)
      `what I wrote to the Minister` IS A `Representations to a Minister` @desc What representations in writing, if any, did you make to a Minister?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my lodged claim deemed discontinued` IS
    `s 16(4)(a) the claim is deemed to be discontinued` `I was dismissed and have lodged a claim for an amount from the dismissal` `what my claim is about` `what I wrote to the Minister`

@export From what date is the claim I lodged deemed discontinued (s 16(4)(b))?
GIVEN `I was dismissed and have lodged a claim for an amount from the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed, and have you lodged a claim for an amount relating to a specified employment dispute that arises from the dismissal?
      `what my claim is about` IS A `Matter of a dispute` @desc What is the claim about?
      `what I wrote to the Minister` IS A `Representations to a Minister` @desc What representations in writing, if any, did you make to a Minister?
      `the day I made the representations` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month did you make the representations?
      `the month I made the representations` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, did you make the representations?
      `the year I made the representations` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year did you make the representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what date is my lodged claim deemed discontinued` IS
    `s 16(4)(b) the date with effect from which the claim is deemed to be discontinued` (`s 16(4)(a) the claim is deemed to be discontinued` `I was dismissed and have lodged a claim for an amount from the dismissal` `what my claim is about` `what I wrote to the Minister`) (`my date` `the day I made the representations` `the month I made the representations` `the year I made the representations`)

-- s 16(5).  After a dismissal you cannot lodge a wrongful dismissal claim if you made representations under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960 and have not withdrawn them, or the Minister has decided.
@export After my dismissal, am I barred from a wrongful dismissal claim because I made representations to the Minister (s 16(5))?
GIVEN `I was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed?
      `my claim is a wrongful dismissal claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim relate to a wrongful dismissal dispute?
      `what I wrote to the Minister` IS A `Representations to a Minister` @desc What representations in writing, if any, did you make to a Minister?
      `I withdrew them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw those representations?
      `the Minister decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister made a decision on those representations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from a wrongful dismissal claim after making representations` IS
    `s 16(5) the employee cannot lodge the claim relating to a wrongful dismissal dispute` `I was dismissed` `my claim is a wrongful dismissal claim` `what I wrote to the Minister` `I withdrew them` `the Minister decided`

-- s 16(6)(a).  If you lodged a wrongful dismissal claim and then made representations under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960, the claim is deemed discontinued.
@export Is the wrongful dismissal claim I lodged deemed discontinued because I then made representations (s 16(6)(a))?
GIVEN `I was dismissed and have lodged a wrongful dismissal claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed, and have you lodged a claim relating to a wrongful dismissal dispute?
      `what I wrote to the Minister` IS A `Representations to a Minister` @desc What representations in writing, if any, did you make to a Minister?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my lodged wrongful dismissal claim deemed discontinued` IS
    `s 16(6)(a) the claim relating to a wrongful dismissal dispute is deemed to be discontinued` `I was dismissed and have lodged a wrongful dismissal claim` `what I wrote to the Minister`

-- s 16(7).  If you made representations under section 8B(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993, you cannot lodge a claim for employment assistance payment unless the Minister allows a mediation request and a certificate is issued.
@export Am I barred from claiming employment assistance payment because I made representations under section 8B(1) (s 16(7))?
GIVEN `I made representations under section 8B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make representations in writing under section 8B(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 to the Minister?
      `the Minister allowed my mediation request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister allow you, under section 8B(7) of that Act, to submit a mediation request about the dispute?
      `a certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a claim referral certificate been issued for that dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from claiming employment assistance payment` IS
    `s 16(7) the employee cannot lodge a claim for employment assistance payment` `I made representations under section 8B(1)` `the Minister allowed my mediation request` `a certificate was issued`

-- s 16(8)(a).  If, after lodging an employment assistance payment claim, you make representations under section 8B(1), the claim is stayed until the Minister decides.
@export Is my employment assistance payment claim stayed because I then made representations (s 16(8)(a))?
GIVEN `I made representations after lodging` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you lodged a claim for employment assistance payment, did you make representations in writing under section 8B(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993?
      `the Minister has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister decided whether to allow the mediation request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment assistance payment claim stayed` IS
    `s 16(8)(a) the claim is stayed` `I made representations after lodging` `the Minister has decided`

-- s 16(8)(c).  If the Minister decides to allow the mediation request, you may proceed with the claim.
@export May I proceed with my employment assistance payment claim once the Minister has decided (s 16(8)(c))?
GIVEN `I made representations after lodging` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you lodged a claim for employment assistance payment, did you make representations in writing under section 8B(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993?
      `the Minister has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister decided whether to allow the mediation request?
      `the Minister allowed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister decide to allow the mediation request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I proceed with my employment assistance payment claim` IS
    `s 16(8)(c) the employee may proceed with the claim` `I made representations after lodging` `the Minister has decided` `the Minister allowed it`

-- s 16(9).  An employer cannot defend an employment assistance payment claim on the ground that you do not meet the re-employment eligibility criteria if the employer did not raise it at the mediation.
@export Can my employer defend my employment assistance payment claim by saying I was not eligible, if they did not say so at the mediation (s 16(9))?
GIVEN `I lodged a claim for employment assistance payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged a claim for employment assistance payment?
      `my employer raised it at the mediation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer raise, during the Part 2 mediation of the dispute about the payment, the ground that you do not satisfy the re-employment eligibility criteria in section 7(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer barred from the eligibility defence` IS
    `s 16(9) the employer cannot defend the claim on the ground that the employee does not satisfy the re-employment eligibility criteria` `I lodged a claim for employment assistance payment` `my employer raised it at the mediation`

-- s 12(1).  Whether the tribunal has jurisdiction to hear the claim: all of s 12(2) to (7) must be satisfied.  This question gathers the person's own answers to the questions above; it is a convenience (ruling E1, option B as hand-gathering guidance only).
@export Does the tribunal have jurisdiction to hear and determine my claim (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `s 12(2) is satisfied` IS A `My answer` @desc Is your claim made by and against the right people (the answer to the question on section 12(2))?
      `s 12(3) is satisfied` IS A `My answer` @desc Is your claim for what the Act allows (section 12(3))?
      `s 12(4) is satisfied` IS A `My answer` @desc Does each amount you claim relate to a specified employment dispute (section 12(4))?
      `s 12(5) is satisfied` IS A `My answer` @desc Is your claim supported by a claim referral certificate for every dispute (section 12(5))?
      `s 12(6) is satisfied` IS A `My answer` @desc Are you in time to lodge your claim (section 12(6))?
      `s 12(7) is satisfied` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the total you claim within the claim limits (section 12(7))?
      `I abandoned the excess` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you abandon the amount over the claim limit (section 15)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the tribunal have jurisdiction over my claim` IS
    `s 12(1) the tribunal has jurisdiction to hear and determine the claim` (`what I say, as a fact` `s 12(2) is satisfied`) (`what I say, as a fact` `s 12(3) is satisfied`) (`what I say, as a fact` `s 12(4) is satisfied`) (`what I say, as a fact` `s 12(5) is satisfied`) (`what I say, as a fact` `s 12(6) is satisfied`) (`what I say, as a fact` `s 12(7) is satisfied`) (`s 15(2)(a) the requirement in section 12(7) is deemed to be satisfied under this paragraph` `I abandoned the excess`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `How do I lodge my claim, and what must come with it? (s 13)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 13(1).  A claim is lodged with a tribunal by filing it with the Registry.
@export Is my claim lodged once I file it with the Registry (s 13(1))?
GIVEN `I filed my claim with the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed your claim with the Registry of the tribunals?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim lodged` IS
    `s 13(1) the claim is lodged with the tribunal` `I filed my claim with the Registry`

-- s 13(2)(a).  Your claim must be filed in the form and manner the Rules of Court prescribe or practice directions specify.
@export Did I file my claim in the form and manner required (s 13(2)(a))?
GIVEN `I used the form and manner in the Rules of Court` IS A `My answer` @desc Did you file your claim in the form and manner that the Rules of Court prescribe?
      `I used the form and manner in a practice direction` IS A `My answer` @desc Did you file your claim in the form and manner that a practice direction of the registrar of the State Courts specifies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I file in the form and manner required` IS
    `s 13(2)(a) the claim is filed in the form and manner required` (`what I say, as a fact` `I used the form and manner in the Rules of Court`) (`what I say, as a fact` `I used the form and manner in a practice direction`)

-- s 13(2)(b)(i).  Your claim must be accompanied by a claim referral certificate for every specified employment dispute it is lodged for.
@export Does a certificate for every dispute come with my claim (s 13(2)(b)(i))?
GIVEN `the number of disputes my claim is lodged for` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many specified employment disputes is your claim lodged?
      `the number of those disputes with a certificate filed` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of them is a claim referral certificate filed with the claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a certificate for every dispute come with my claim` IS
    `s 13(2)(b)(i) the claim is accompanied by a claim referral certificate for every specified employment dispute` `the number of disputes my claim is lodged for` `the number of those disputes with a certificate filed`

-- s 13(2)(b)(ii).  Your claim must be accompanied by any other documents the Rules of Court or practice directions require.
@export Do all the other documents required come with my claim (s 13(2)(b)(ii))?
GIVEN `every other document required is filed` IS A `My answer` @desc Is every other document that the Rules of Court prescribe, or a practice direction specifies, filed with your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the other required documents come with my claim` IS
    `s 13(2)(b)(ii) the claim is accompanied by the other documents required` (`what I say, as a fact` `every other document required is filed`)

-- s 13(2)(b)(iii).  Your claim must be accompanied by the court fee, if any, that the Rules of Court prescribe.
@export Is the court fee I am paying with my claim enough (s 13(2)(b)(iii))?
GIVEN `the court fee I am paying` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, are you paying as the court fee with your claim?
      `the court fee the Rules of Court prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What court fee, in dollars, do the Rules of Court prescribe for your claim? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my court fee enough` IS
    `s 13(2)(b)(iii) the claim is accompanied by the court fee prescribed` `the court fee I am paying` (`my amount if I know it` `the court fee the Rules of Court prescribe`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `At the hearing: representation, privacy, evidence and burden of proof (ss 18 to 21 and 27)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 19(1) to (3).  At the tribunal you act in person and cannot be represented by an advocate and solicitor or by an agent, except as s 19(2) and (3) allow.
@export Can this person represent me, or the other side, at the tribunal (s 19(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `who the party is` IS A `Kind of party` @desc Who is the party to be represented? (an individual; the Government; a body corporate; a partnership; an unincorporated association)
      `who would represent the party` IS A `Kind of representative` @desc Who would represent the party?
      `the regulations prescribe this representative for this party` IS A `My answer` @desc Do the regulations made under section 34 prescribe this individual as a representative for this party? (Answer only if the representative is "another individual prescribed by regulations".)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this person represent a party at the tribunal` IS
    `s 19(1) to (3) the party may be represented before the tribunal by the representative` `who the party is` `who would represent the party` (`what I say, as a fact` `the regulations prescribe this representative for this party`)

-- s 18(1).  All proceedings before a tribunal are conducted in private.
@export Will the proceedings on my claim be conducted in private (s 18(1))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are before a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings before an Employment Claims Tribunal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the proceedings on my claim private` IS
    `s 18(1) the proceedings before the tribunal are conducted in private` `the proceedings are before a tribunal`

-- s 18(4).  The tribunal may permit a prescribed individual, a member of a prescribed class, or anyone else it deems fit to observe the hearing.
@export May the tribunal let this person observe my hearing (s 18(4))?
GIVEN `the person is prescribed or in a prescribed class` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the person an individual whom the regulations prescribe, or who belongs to a class that the regulations prescribe, for observing a hearing?
      `the tribunal deems the person fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tribunal deem the person fit to observe the hearing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tribunal let this person observe` IS
    `s 18(4) the tribunal may permit the individual to observe the hearing of the claim` (`what I say, as a fact` `the person is prescribed or in a prescribed class`) `the tribunal deems the person fit`

-- s 20(8).  If a party without reasonable excuse fails to attend, the tribunal may hear the claim and decide in that party's absence.
@export May the tribunal decide my claim without me if I do not turn up (s 20(8))?
GIVEN `I fail to attend without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you (or the other party) fail, without reasonable excuse, to attend the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tribunal decide in my absence` IS
    `s 20(8) the tribunal may hear the claim and make its decision in the absence of the party` `I fail to attend without reasonable excuse`

-- s 20(7).  For a wrongful dismissal claim, the tribunal is to have regard to the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal, and to calculate any compensation under the regulations.
@export Must the tribunal have regard to the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal (s 20(7)(a))?
GIVEN `my claim involves a wrongful dismissal dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tribunal deciding a claim involving a wrongful dismissal dispute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the tribunal have regard to the wrongful dismissal guidelines` IS
    `s 20(7)(a) the tribunal is to have regard to the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal` `my claim involves a wrongful dismissal dispute`

-- s 21(2).  The tribunal may draw inferences from an employer's failure to comply with an obligation under a written law in the Fourth Schedule, including that missing evidence would have been unfavourable to the employer.
@export May the tribunal draw an inference against my employer because it did not meet an obligation it had (s 21(2))?
GIVEN `what the obligation was` IS A `Obligation of a party under a written law` @desc Which obligation did the party fail to meet? (an obligation under the Fourth Schedule, such as an employer's obligation under section 95, 95A or 96 of the Employment Act 1968, or an obligation under the Employment of Foreign Manpower (Work Passes) Regulations 2012; or some other obligation)
      `the party failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the party fail to comply with that obligation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tribunal draw an inference from the failure` IS
    `s 21(2) the tribunal may draw any inference it thinks fit from the party's failure` `what the obligation was` `the party failed to comply`

-- s 21(3).  Evidence need not be given on oath or affirmation, unless the tribunal requires it.
@export Do I have to give my evidence on oath (s 21(3))?
GIVEN `the tribunal requires evidence on oath or affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the tribunal required your evidence to be given on oath or affirmation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Need my evidence be on oath` IS
    `s 21(3) the evidence need not be given on oath or affirmation` `the tribunal requires evidence on oath or affirmation`

-- s 21(6).  All evidence and information the tribunal obtained on its own initiative must be disclosed to every party.
@export Must the tribunal tell me what evidence it found itself (s 21(6))?
GIVEN `the tribunal found the evidence itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the tribunal obtain the evidence or information itself, on its own initiative, under section 21(5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the tribunal disclose what it found` IS
    `s 21(6) the evidence and information must be disclosed to every party to the proceedings` `the tribunal found the evidence itself`

-- s 27(1).  A person who alleges that they are not the employer or employee of the claimant, or not a person with a duty under one of three Acts, bears the burden of proving it.
@export Who must prove an allegation that someone is not the employer or the employee (s 27(1))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court?
      `the allegation` IS AN `Allegation about a duty or a relationship` @desc What is alleged? (that the person is not the employer or employee of the claimant; that the person is not a person with a duty under the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001, the Employment Act 1968 or the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993; or something else)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the person who alleges it bear the burden` IS
    `s 27(1) the person who makes the allegation bears the burden of proving it` `the proceedings are under the Act` `the allegation`

-- s 27(2)(a).  If an employee is dismissed without notice and claims under section 14(2) of the Employment Act 1968, the employer must prove the dismissal was with just cause or excuse.
@export If I was dismissed without notice, must my employer prove it had just cause (s 27(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court?
      `I was dismissed without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed without notice under section 14(1) of the Employment Act 1968?
      `I lodged a claim under section 14(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of that Act against the employer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer prove just cause` IS
    `s 27(2)(a) the employer bears the burden of proving that the employee was dismissed with just cause or excuse` `the proceedings are under the Act` `I was dismissed without notice` `I lodged a claim under section 14(2)`

-- s 27(2)(b).  If an employee is dismissed with notice on the ground of poor performance or misconduct, the employer must prove that ground.
@export If I was dismissed with notice for poor performance or misconduct, must my employer prove that (s 27(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court?
      `I was dismissed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you dismissed with notice?
      `the notice gave poor performance or misconduct as the ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice of dismissal given (or does it purport to be given) on the ground of poor performance or misconduct by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer prove the ground for the notice` IS
    `s 27(2)(b) the employer bears the burden of proving the ground for giving the notice of dismissal` `the proceedings are under the Act` `I was dismissed with notice` `the notice gave poor performance or misconduct as the ground`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What the tribunal can order, and what it can cost me (s 22)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 22(1).  A tribunal may determine a claim within its jurisdiction by ordering payment of money, dismissing the claim, ordering costs, or ordering reinstatement.
@export May the tribunal make this order on my claim (s 22(1))?
GIVEN `the tribunal has jurisdiction over my claim` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the claim within the tribunal's jurisdiction (the answer to the question on section 12(1))?
      `the order` IS AN `Order of a tribunal` @desc What order is asked for? (to pay money to another party; to dismiss the whole or part of the claim; to pay costs to another party; to reinstate an employee in the former employment; or another kind of order)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tribunal make this order` IS
    `s 22(1) the tribunal may make the order` (`what I say, as a fact` `the tribunal has jurisdiction over my claim`) `the order`

-- s 22(2).  In deciding on costs the tribunal may take into account a frivolous or vexatious claim, or a party's failure without reasonable excuse to attend a mediation or the proceedings.
@export May the tribunal take this into account when deciding whether to order me to pay costs (s 22(2))?
GIVEN `the claim was frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the claim frivolous or vexatious?
      `a party missed a mediation without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a party, without reasonable excuse, fail to attend a mediation under Part 2, or a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator, of a dispute the claim is lodged for?
      `a party missed the proceedings without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a party, without reasonable excuse, fail to attend proceedings before the tribunal that the party was required to attend?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tribunal take this into account on costs` IS
    `s 22(2) the tribunal may take the matter into account in deciding whether to make a costs order` `the claim was frivolous or vexatious` `a party missed a mediation without reasonable excuse` `a party missed the proceedings without reasonable excuse`

-- s 22(4).  The total ordered to be paid to a party for salary-type disputes must not exceed the prescribed claim limit.
@export Is the total the tribunal orders for salary-type disputes within the claim limit (s 22(4))?
GIVEN `the total ordered for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What total, in dollars, is ordered to be paid for every specified contractual dispute and every specified statutory dispute?
      `my claim limit for salary-type disputes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed claim limit in section 12(7)(a) that applies to the party, in dollars? (0 if you do not know)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the total ordered within the claim limit` IS
    `s 22(4) the total ordered to be paid for contractual and statutory disputes is within the claim limit` `the total ordered for salary-type disputes` (`my amount if I know it` `my claim limit for salary-type disputes`)

-- s 22(6)(a) and (b).  Costs are not part of the money ordered under (1)(a), and a payment is applied first to the amount, then to the costs.
@export How much of the total I am ordered to pay is the amount, leaving out costs (s 22(6)(a))?
GIVEN `the total I am ordered to pay, costs included` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total, in dollars, you are ordered to pay, costs included?
      `the costs I am ordered to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that, in dollars, is costs under section 22(1)(c)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the total is the amount without costs` IS
    `s 22(6)(a) the amount of money ordered under subsection (1)(a), which does not include costs` `the total I am ordered to pay, costs included` `the costs I am ordered to pay`

@export How much of what I have paid goes to the amount, and how much to the costs (s 22(6)(b))?
GIVEN `what I have paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, have you paid so far?
      `the amount I am ordered to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, are you ordered to pay under section 22(1)(a)?
      `the costs I am ordered to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What costs, in dollars, are you ordered to pay under section 22(1)(c)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of what I paid is applied to the amount` IS
    `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the amount under subsection (1)(a)` `what I have paid` `the amount I am ordered to pay`

@export How much of what I have paid is applied to the costs (s 22(6)(b))?
GIVEN `what I have paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in dollars, have you paid so far?
      `the amount I am ordered to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in dollars, are you ordered to pay under section 22(1)(a)?
      `the costs I am ordered to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What costs, in dollars, are you ordered to pay under section 22(1)(c)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of what I paid is applied to the costs` IS
    `s 22(6)(b) the part of the payment applied to the costs under subsection (1)(c)` `what I have paid` `the amount I am ordered to pay` `the costs I am ordered to pay`

-- s 22(7).  A claim, or part of a claim, over which the tribunal has no jurisdiction must be dismissed for lack of jurisdiction.
@export Must the tribunal dismiss my claim because it has no jurisdiction (s 22(7))?
GIVEN `the tribunal has no jurisdiction over the claim or the part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tribunal have no jurisdiction to determine the claim, or a part of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the tribunal dismiss for lack of jurisdiction` IS
    `s 22(7) the claim or the part must be dismissed for lack of jurisdiction` `the tribunal has no jurisdiction over the claim or the part`

-- s 22(8).  Instead of making an order, the tribunal may refer the dispute back to mediation, with or without the parties' consent.
@export Can the tribunal send my dispute back to mediation instead of deciding it (s 22(8))?
GIVEN `where my claim came from` IS A `Where a claim arose` @desc Did your claim arise from a mediation under Part 2, or from a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator, or from neither?
      `the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the parties consent to the referral? (The Act allows it with or without consent.)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of mediation referred to`
DECIDE `To what kind of mediation can the tribunal refer my dispute` IS
    `s 22(8) the kind of mediation the tribunal may refer the dispute to` `where my claim came from` `the parties consent`

-- s 22(10).  The tribunal may correct an order within 14 days after it is made.  This gives the last day.
@export By what date may the tribunal correct its order (s 22(10))?
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was the order made (or the statement of grounds issued)?
      `the month the order was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month, from 1 to 12, was it made?
      `the year the order was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year was it made?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date may the tribunal correct its order` IS
    `s 22(10) the last day on which the tribunal may make the correction` (`my date` `the day the order was made` `the month the order was made` `the year the order was made`)

-- s 22(12).  A tribunal's order may be enforced in the same manner as a District Court judgment.
@export Can a tribunal's order be enforced like a District Court judgment (s 22(12))?
GIVEN `the order was made by a tribunal under section 22(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made by a tribunal under section 22(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the tribunal order be enforced like a judgment` IS
    `s 22(12) the order may be enforced in the same manner as a judgment given or an order made by a District Court` `the order was made by a tribunal under section 22(1)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `If I want to appeal, or the other side does (ss 23 to 26)`
-- Situation: asked only after the tribunal has made an order.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 23(1) and (2).  A party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court on a question of law, or on the ground that the claim was outside the tribunal's jurisdiction, but only if a District Court gives permission.
@export Can I appeal against the tribunal's order (s 23(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the proceedings before the tribunal?
      `the order is a section 22(1) order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made by the tribunal under section 22(1)?
      `my ground` IS A `Ground of appeal` @desc What is your ground of appeal? (a question of law; that the claim was outside the tribunal's jurisdiction; a question of fact; or another ground)
      `a District Court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a District Court given you permission to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I appeal` IS
    `s 23(1) and (2) an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` (`s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` `I am a party to the proceedings` `the order is a section 22(1) order` `my ground`) (`s 23(2) the condition that a District Court gives permission to appeal is met` `a District Court gave permission`)

-- s 23(4).  A District Court's order giving or refusing permission, extending or refusing to extend time for correction, or remitting or refusing to remit, is final.
@export Is the District Court's order on my appeal final (s 23(4))?
GIVEN `the District Court's order` IS AN `Order of a District Court on an appeal` @desc What did the District Court order? (give or refuse permission to appeal; extend or refuse to extend the time for correcting the tribunal's order; remit or refuse to remit the matter to the tribunal; or another order)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the District Court order final` IS
    `s 23(4) the order is final and is not subject to any appeal` `the District Court's order`

-- s 24(1).  An appeal does not by itself stop the order from being executed or enforced, unless a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders otherwise.
@export Does my appeal stop the tribunal's order being enforced against me (s 24(1))?
GIVEN `a court has ordered a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a District Court or the General Division of the High Court ordered otherwise (a stay of execution or enforcement)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my appeal stop enforcement by itself` IS
    `s 24(1) the appeal by itself operates as a stay of execution or enforcement of the order` `a court has ordered a stay`

-- s 24(1), the other half.  An appeal does not operate as a stay unless a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders otherwise, so enforcement is stayed pending an appeal where a court orders a stay.
@export Is enforcement of the order stayed while the appeal is pending (s 24(1))?
GIVEN `an appeal has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an appeal been brought against the tribunal's order under section 22(1)?
      `a court has ordered a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a District Court or the General Division of the High Court ordered a stay of execution or enforcement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is enforcement stayed while I appeal` IS
    `s 24(1) execution or enforcement of the order is stayed pending the appeal` `an appeal has been brought` `a court has ordered a stay`

-- s 24(4).  The General Division of the High Court may order a stay only if a District Court has given permission to appeal and no stay application was made to a District Court.
@export Can the High Court order a stay of the order against me (s 24(4))?
GIVEN `permission to appeal was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a District Court given permission to appeal against the order?
      `a stay was applied for in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an application made to any District Court for a stay of execution or enforcement of the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the conditions for a High Court stay met` IS
    `s 24(4) the conditions for the General Division of the High Court to order a stay are met` `permission to appeal was given` `a stay was applied for in a District Court`

-- s 26.  The General Division of the High Court's decision on an appeal, or on a stay application, is final.
@export Is the High Court's decision final (s 26)?
GIVEN `what the High Court decided` IS A `Matter decided by the General Division of the High Court` @desc What did the General Division of the High Court decide? (an appeal against a tribunal's order; an application for a stay; or something else)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the High Court decision final` IS
    `s 26 the judgment, order or direction of the General Division of the High Court is final` `what the High Court decided`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Can my contract stop me, and who may see my information? (ss 28 to 31)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 28.  A provision in an agreement is void to the extent that it purports to exclude or limit a tribunal's jurisdiction, or to stop you submitting a mediation request or making a claim, application or appeal.
@export Is a term in my contract that stops me from claiming void (s 28)?
GIVEN `what the term purports to do` IS A `What a provision of an agreement purports to do` @desc What does the term purport to do? (exclude or limit the jurisdiction of a tribunal; prevent you from submitting a mediation request; prevent you from making a claim, application or appeal under this Act; or something else)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the term in my agreement void` IS
    `s 28 the provision in the agreement is void to that extent` `what the term purports to do`

-- s 29(1).  The Commissioner, an approved mediator, a tribunal magistrate or a Registrar may disclose information about a mediation request, a mediation, a claim or tribunal proceedings, for one of the purposes in s 29(1)(a) to (f).
@export May the Commissioner, the mediator, the tribunal magistrate or the Registrar share information about my claim (s 29(1))?
GIVEN `who would share it` IS A `Person who may disclose under section 29` @desc Who would share the information? (the Commissioner; an approved mediator; a tribunal magistrate; a Registrar; or someone else who holds information)
      `to administer the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure necessary for or in connection with the administration or execution of the Act?
      `to give me financial or social assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure necessary for providing financial or social assistance to the claimant or the respondent?
      `to help a law enforcement agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made to assist a law enforcement agency in investigating an offence under any written law?
      `to a public agency for policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made to a public agency for the purpose of policy formulation or review?
      `to a public agency in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure made to a public agency and necessary in the public interest?
      `for another prescribed purpose` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the disclosure made for any other purpose that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May information about my claim be shared` IS
    `s 29(1) the person may disclose the information` `who would share it` `to administer the Act` `to give me financial or social assistance` `to help a law enforcement agency` `to a public agency for policy` `to a public agency in the public interest` (`what I say, as a fact` `for another prescribed purpose`)

-- s 29(2).  A tribunal magistrate or a Registrar may publish information about a tribunal's order or decision.
@export May the tribunal publish its order or decision on my claim (s 29(2))?
GIVEN `who would publish it` IS A `Person who may disclose under section 29` @desc Who would publish the information?
      `it is about an order or decision of a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to an order or a decision of a tribunal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tribunal publish its decision on my claim` IS
    `s 29(2) the person may publish the information` `who would publish it` `it is about an order or decision of a tribunal`

-- s 30(3).  No liability lies personally against the Commissioner, an authorised individual or an approved mediator who acts in good faith and with reasonable care.
@export Can I make the mediator or the Commissioner personally liable for what they did (s 30(3))?
GIVEN `who I would hold liable` IS A `Person protected under section 30(3)` @desc Whom would you hold liable? (the Commissioner; an individual authorised to carry out a function or duty of the Commissioner; an approved mediator; or someone else)
      `they acted in good faith and with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person act in good faith and with reasonable care in doing or omitting to do the thing, in the execution or purported execution of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the mediator or Commissioner protected from personal liability` IS
    `s 30(3) no liability lies personally against the person` `who I would hold liable` `they acted in good faith and with reasonable care`
